2. Definitions

"Affiliate" means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
common control with the Licensee.

"Authorized Personnel" means the Licensee's employees and individual
contractors who access the Licensed Code solely on the Licensee's behalf, are
bound by confidentiality and use restrictions at least as protective as this
License, and do not use the Licensed Code for their own or another customer's
benefit.

"Commercial Agreement" means the applicable Zeep Orbit Commercial
Subscription Terms, order form, checkout terms, invoice, or other written
commercial agreement accepted by the Licensee.

"Competing Offering" means a product or service made available to third
parties that substitutes for Zeep Orbit, offers Zeep Orbit itself as a hosted
or managed service, or provides the same or substantially similar backend
platform, BaaS, PaaS, administrative APIs, dashboard, or enterprise
functionality as a commercial service.

"Enterprise License Key" means an active cryptographically signed license key
issued by the Licensor under a Commercial Agreement.

"Reseller License Key" means an Enterprise License Key expressly designated
by the Licensor, under a separate written Commercial Agreement covering
resale or hosting rights, as authorizing the specific Competing Offering
described in that Commercial Agreement. A standard Enterprise License Key
issued for a Licensee's own internal use is not a Reseller License Key and
does not authorize any activity described in Section 6.

"Licensee" means the individual or single legal entity that acquired the
applicable Enterprise License Key. Affiliates are not Licensees unless they
separately acquire a key or are expressly included in an order form.

"Non-Production Environment" means an environment used exclusively for
internal evaluation, development, automated testing, continuous integration,
staging, demonstration, or acceptance testing, and not used to provide live
services or production workloads to end users or customers.

"Production Environment" means any environment used to provide live services,
process production workloads or data, support ordinary business operations, or
make functionality available to end users or customers.

