4. Production Grant

While the Licensee holds a valid Enterprise License Key, the Licensor grants
the Licensee a worldwide, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable, and terminable right to compile, install, deploy, and run the
Licensed Code in Production Environments for the Licensee's own internal
business operations and for software products or services operated by the
Licensee that do not constitute a Competing Offering.

Unless an order form expressly states otherwise, the Production Grant is not
limited by number of users, seats, applications, projects, servers, clusters,
instances, environments, or end users, provided every installation is owned or
controlled by the same Licensee and complies with this License.

The Licensed Code may be deployed on infrastructure located in any country,
subject to applicable law, sanctions, export controls, and provider
restrictions.

5. Permitted Customer Products and Professional Services

The Licensee may use Zeep Orbit, including the Licensed Code, as internal
infrastructure to build and operate its own websites, applications, APIs, and
software-as-a-service products. A product does not become a Competing Offering
merely because it is a SaaS product that uses Zeep Orbit as an internal
technology component.

A contractor or service provider may install, configure, maintain, or operate
Zeep Orbit solely on behalf of a Licensee that holds its own Enterprise License
Key. The contractor or service provider may not reuse that key or installation
for another customer.

6. Prohibited Competitive Use

The Licensee may not, directly or indirectly, unless expressly authorized by a
Reseller License Key:

a. make the Licensed Code or its enterprise functionality available as part
   of a Competing Offering;

b. offer Zeep Orbit hosting, managed Zeep Orbit, backend-as-a-service,
   platform-as-a-service, white-label, OEM, resale, or substantially similar
   services to third parties using the Licensed Code;

c. allow third parties to create, administer, or operate their own independent
   Orbit tenants, projects, or backend environments as customers of a hosted
   or managed Orbit service; or

d. use one Enterprise License Key to provide Zeep Orbit installations or
   managed services to multiple independent customers.

A standard Enterprise License Key issued for internal use never authorizes
any activity in this Section 6. Any use that may reasonably constitute a
Competing Offering requires a Reseller License Key issued under a separate
written commercial agreement with the Licensor.

