9. License Key, Subscription, and Grace Period

Enterprise License Keys are issued under a Commercial Agreement. Subscription
term, price, billing, automatic renewal, cancellation, grace period, and other
commercial conditions are governed by that Commercial Agreement. A Reseller
License Key is issued under a distinct Commercial Agreement covering resale
or hosting rights and does not share the terms of a standard Enterprise
License Key unless that agreement says so.

Signed metadata embedded in an Enterprise License Key implements and evidences
the applicable Commercial Agreement but does not amend or supersede it.

Unless a Commercial Agreement states otherwise, a seven-calendar-day grace
period applies after a subscription expires or a renewal payment fails. During
the grace period, Production Use may continue. After the grace period, the
Production Grant automatically suspends until payment and key status are
regularized.

Suspension or expiration affects only enterprise functionality. It does not
terminate MIT License rights for the rest of the repository and must not, by
itself, delete Licensee data.

